{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>And the fast of the fifth:</b> as I mentioned, on the tenth of the month." "<b>And the fast of the seventh:</b> The number of days of the month is not written, and the disputants said: it is the day they fasted at the end of the festival of Sukkot in Ezra, and they are mistaken, for then they fasted on account of the transgression of the exile, and it is not written there that evil came upon Israel." "<b>In the seventh month:</b> only the matter of Gedaliah. And it is written: \"And it came to pass in the seventh month,\" and since the days of the month were not specified, it is possible that it was at the beginning of the month, the lunar month, like \"new moon and sabbath, in the third month after the children of Israel went out\"; and since Scripture says \"on the first of the month,\" this is said for reinforcement, so that it will not arise in the listener's heart that it is not the first day, for Scripture says \"your new moons and your appointed times,\" and there is no argument from the phrase \"and at your new moons,\" for those are the months of Nisan, and it is written there: \"burnt-offering of the new moon in its month,\" and from received tradition we receive: \"and on the day of your rejoicing and on your appointed times and at your new moons.\" If so, Gedaliah was killed on Rosh HaShanah; therefore they fixed it on the third day, or they received it thus from the holy fathers." "<b>And the fast of the tenth:</b> It is written in Ezekiel: \"Write for yourself the name of the day.\" Now, our Sages, of blessed memory, left the fast of the seventh and the tenth as they were formerly, and because on the seventeenth of Tammuz the priests were killed in the house of HaShem, and five things happened on it, they fixed it as a fast but did not burden the public to fast on the ninth; and on the day of the ninth of Av Jerusalem was captured also a second time, and the First Temple was burned on it — they fixed it. And Scripture did not mention the fast of Esther, and the time of Ahasuerus had already passed, for it is not written in the scroll on which day the fast is fixed, for all Israel fasted three days in Nisan. And in the verse \"the words of the fasts and their cry,\" its meaning is not as many thought, and thus is its meaning: they fulfilled and accepted upon themselves the days of Purim to rejoice in them; even though the prophets did not command them, the sons are obligated to do what their fathers accepted, just as they accepted upon themselves these four fasts mentioned, which were not from the mouth of a prophet. Now, the answer regarding these days, in which they were weeping and mourning: days of gladness and joy, and they shall keep the commandments of HaShem according to the prophets, and this is: \"and love truth and peace,\" as it is written: \"truth and judgment of peace.\" And this answer that the prophet gave is against those who asked, \"Should I weep in the fifth month,\" who were not keeping the Torah that HaShem commanded, and were asking whether they should keep what their fathers accepted upon themselves. Now, the prophet answered: you would do better if you would heed the words of HaShem and leave the words of the fathers, than if you keep the words of the fathers and leave the words of HaShem — they are the perfect righteous."], :book :zechariah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {2 "The biblical quotation 'ובאחד לחדש' ('on the first of the month') is not from the Gedaliah narrative in Jeremiah 41 but appears invoked here as prooftext; the argument is compressed and the exact referent is ambiguous.", 3 "The phrase 'ובדברי הכתוב: דברי הצומות וזעקתם' is ambiguous: it may refer to a scriptural verse containing these words or to 'matters of Scripture' generally; the following interpretation links it to the Purim verse קיימו וקבלו (Esther 9:27), but the syntactic transition is compressed and the argument is difficult to parse with certainty."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Zecharia -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/zecharya"] ["1" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=25&perek=5&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:46:37.412714614Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}